  "term": "stria vascularis",
  "definition": "The stria vascularis is a vascularized epithelial structure in the cochlea of the inner ear. In this source, its development is described as being delayed and its cells stretched in mice lacking functional pendrin, linking abnormal stria vascularis development to deafness.",
