      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that the stria vascularis is “a vascularized epithelial structure in the cochlea,” but the packet excerpt does not explicitly define stria vascularis this way; it only reports that “structural development of stria vascularis, including vascularization, was retarded” (i.e., vascularization is mentioned, but not the full stated structural characterization as an epithelial cochlear structure).",
        "The definition’s overall description is largely consistent with the packet (delayed/retarded development and epithelial cell stretching in Slc26a4 −/− mice, and possible linkage to deafness), but because the first substantive structural characterization is not directly supported by the provided text, the definition is not fully defensible."
